book_054,The White Ribbon,Neville Wright Poulsom,ol1637821a,Khoa học viễn tưởng,This book is an important source of information about the Arctic and Polar Medals which were awarded by Great Britain in the period 1818 to 1961. It gives brief accounts of the expeditions themselves and lists the names of the recipients of the medals.  The medals are described and illustrated by black-and-white photographs.,1968,0900652004,B.A.Seaby Ltd,216,Tiếng Anh,"Hardcover, black cloth, endpaper maps",https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7243992-L.jpg,0.0,False,"Medals, Arctic and Antarctic Expeditions",,,,,False,,,,,
book_065,Of Mice and Men,John Steinbeck,ol25788a,Khoa học viễn tưởng,"The second book in John Steinbeck’s labor trilogy, Of Mice and Men is a touching tale of two migrant laborers in search of work and eventual liberation from their social circumstances. Fiercely devoted to one another, George and Lennie plan to save up to finance their dream of someday owning a small piece of land. The pair seems unstoppable until tragedy strikes and their hopes come crashing down, forcing George to make a difficult decision regarding the welfare of his best friend.

The novel is set on a ranch in Soledad, CA. Author Frank Bergon recalls reading Of Mice and Men for the first time as a teenager living in the San Joaquin Valley and remembers how he saw “as if in a jolt of light the ordinary surroundings of [his] life become worthy of literature.” Steinbeck works to propagate the notion that meaningful stories emerge from the marginalized; that even those on the fringes of society can make deserving contributions to the literary canon.

Source: http://www.steinbeck.org/about-john/his-works/


