book_115,Kitty's Class Day and Other Stories,Louisa May Alcott,ol26680a,Khoa học viễn tưởng,"From the book:""A stitch in time saves nine.""  ""O Pris, Pris, I'm really going! Here's the invitation – rough paper - Chapel - spreads - Lyceum Hall - everything splendid; and Jack to take care of me!""  As Kitty burst into the room and performed a rapturous pas seul, waving the cards over her head, sister Priscilla looked up from her work with a smile of satisfaction on her quiet face.",1908,9781647995195,Bibliotech Press,178,Tiếng Anh,,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2812701-L.jpg,0.0,False,"Classic Literature, Fiction, Balls (Parties), Cross-cousin marriage, Juvenile literature, Evening gowns, Pride and vanity, Fiction, short stories (single author), Children's stories, Children's stories, American, Conduct of life, Family, Fiction, general, Young women, Juvenile fiction, Brothers and sisters, Young men, Wealth, Artists, Proverbs",,,,,False,,,,,
