4b9a24ce,Are we Ruined by the Germans?,Harold Cox,,Business & Personal Finance,"In this book, an attempt is made to show that British trade is being knocked to pieces by German competition, that already the sun has set on England's commercial supremacy, and that if British are not careful the few crumbs of trade still left.",1936,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication1/v4/f0/4b/4e/f04b4e89-2b55-f8c2-6df7-364741ad5463/coverArt.871430.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,tài chính,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"In this book, an attempt is made to show that British trade is being knocked to pieces by German competition, that already the sun has set on England's commercial supremacy, and that if British are not careful the few crumbs of trade still left.",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/are-we-ruined-by-the-germans/id511255005?uo=4,
d594bedc,The Caxtons — Volume 08,Edward Bulwer-Lytton,,Personal Finance,"My little cousin now slipped from my father's arms, and, running up the stairs, beckoned to us to follow. We did so, and were led to a door, at which the child stopped and listened; then, taking off her shoes, she stole in on tiptoe. We entered after her.",1873,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/2e/92/dc/2e92dc34-0948-5c52-cfff-548dad35ade6/coverArt.f92fd8.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,tài chính,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"My little cousin now slipped from my father's arms, and, running up the stairs, beckoned to us to follow. We did so, and were led to a door, at which the child stopped and listened; then, taking off her shoes, she stole in on tiptoe. We entered after her.",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/the-caxtons-volume-08/id506069531?uo=4,
5d9954f7,Esther,Henry Adams,,Contemporary Romance,"The plot of this novel concerns a freethinking young woman’s encounter, through artistic pursuits, with a church, an experienced artist, and a orphan woman from the West.  As Esther incorporates herself into this world, she agrees to marry the preacher, Mr. Hazard.  She is all but an atheist.  Her close friend, George, is a paleontologist and agnostic.  Her father uses religion only for its moral influence on society, not out of any true believe.  Esther is never quite able to resolve her conflict between her love for Mr. Hazard (admitted in the final line of the novel) and her disgust with her finance’s beliefs and practices.  The idea of being a church wife, attending services and putting on the face of a devoted believer disgusts her.",1878,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication5/v4/de/87/d4/de87d43e-7987-9b54-aa04-a730a2364269/coverArt.5967f2.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,tài chính,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"The plot of this novel concerns a freethinking young woman’s encounter, through artistic pursuits, with a church, an experienced artist, and a orphan woman from the West.  As Esther incorporates herself into this world, she agrees to marry the preacher, Mr. Hazard.  She is all but an atheist.  Her close friend, George, is a paleontologist and agnostic.  Her father uses religion only for its moral influence on society, not out of any true believe.  Esther is never quite able to resolve her confli...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/esther/id508683934?uo=4,
