243c3045,The Market-Place,Harold Frederic,,Fiction & Literature,"This is a novel book. The Market Place project for young people has been established in Leeds since 1989. It is a respected provider of young people’s counselling… Here you can find out about the different services available at The Market Place, which is based in Leeds City Centre. Services at The Market Place are free and confidential, and available to 13-25 year olds in Leeds.",1898,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/6a/40/28/6a402884-df6d-367e-4705-f180ee47cc90/coverArt.b1c5f1.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"This is a novel book. The Market Place project for young people has been established in Leeds since 1989. It is a respected provider of young people’s counselling… Here you can find out about the different services available at The Market Place, which is based in Leeds City Centre. Services at The Market Place are free and confidential, and available to 13-25 year olds in Leeds.",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/the-market-place/id498718245?uo=4,
1068439f,The Investment of Influence,Newell Dwight Hillis,,Philosophy,"Philosophical book which says that how the glory of our fathers was their emphasis of the principle of self care and self culture. Finding that he who first made the most of himself was best fitted to make something of others, the teachers of yesterday unceasingly plied men with motives of personal responsibility. Influenced by the former generation, our age has organized the principle of individualism into its home, its school, its market place and forum. By reason of the increase in gold, books, travel and personal luxuries, some now feel that selfness is beginning to degenerate into selfishness. The time, therefore, seems to have fully come when the principle of self care should receive its complement through the principle of care for others. These chapters assert the debt of wealth to poverty, the debt of wisdom to ignorance, the debt of strength to weakness. If ""A Man's Value to Society"" affirms the duty of self culture and character, these studies emphasize the law of social sympathy and social service.",1929,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication1/v4/44/02/f3/4402f3d4-51cb-e4b4-c35b-528ddf4df32e/coverArt.b64cb4.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"Philosophical book which says that how the glory of our fathers was their emphasis of the principle of self care and self culture. Finding that he who first made the most of himself was best fitted to make something of others, the teachers of yesterday unceasingly plied men with motives of personal responsibility. Influenced by the former generation, our age has organized the principle of individualism into its home, its school, its market place and forum. By reason of the increase in gold, book...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/the-investment-of-influence/id510871935?uo=4,
9eb08f8f,"Goblin Market, The Prince's Progress, and Other Poems",Christina Georgina Rossetti,,Poetry,"Goblin Market"" (composed in April 1859 and published in 1862) is a narrative poem by&#xa0;Christina Rossetti. In a letter to her publisher, Rossetti claimed that the poem, which is interpreted frequently as having features of remarkably sexual imagery, was not meant for children. However, in public Rossetti often stated that the poem&#xa0;was&#xa0;intended for children, and went on to write many children's poems. When the poem appeared in her first volume of poetry,&#xa0;Goblin Market and Other Poems, it was illustrated by her brother, the&#xa0;Pre-Raphaelite artist&#xa0;Dante Gabriel Rossetti.",1894,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication5/v4/26/6d/49/266d4909-cd2a-f41d-6262-20a992c4c914/coverArt.9f5f55.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"Goblin Market"" (composed in April 1859 and published in 1862) is a narrative poem by&#xa0;Christina Rossetti. In a letter to her publisher, Rossetti claimed that the poem, which is interpreted frequently as having features of remarkably sexual imagery, was not meant for children. However, in public Rossetti often stated that the poem&#xa0;was&#xa0;intended for children, and went on to write many children's poems. When the poem appeared in her first volume of poetry,&#xa0;Goblin Market and Other ...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/goblin-market-the-princes-progress-and-other-poems/id510935313?uo=4,
d8bbfff2,Some One Like You,James William Foley,,Erotica,"Halley and Scarlett Thomas live in directly opposite houses and both had jobs at Milton's Market. At the beginning of the summer, Scarlett started dating Michael Sherwood but they decide to keep it quiet, with only Halley really knowing.",1939,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/b6/40/2b/b6402bbc-5bba-be16-6dcf-ba5937f0dcf3/coverArt.799174.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"Halley and Scarlett Thomas live in directly opposite houses and both had jobs at Milton's Market. At the beginning of the summer, Scarlett started dating Michael Sherwood but they decide to keep it quiet, with only Halley really knowing.",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/some-one-like-you/id510930595?uo=4,
851b19f7,Poems,Christina Georgina Rossetti,,Poetry,"She was an English poet who wrote a variety of romantic, devotional, and children's poems. She is perhaps best known for her long poem Goblin Market, her love poem Remember, and for the words of the Christmas carol In the Bleak Midwinter.",1894,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication5/v4/b1/2f/f4/b12ff42b-5f49-bac0-bed2-a428f1c58449/coverArt.63ed74.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"She was an English poet who wrote a variety of romantic, devotional, and children's poems. She is perhaps best known for her long poem Goblin Market, her love poem Remember, and for the words of the Christmas carol In the Bleak Midwinter.",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/poems/id511006120?uo=4,
7bc98dea,Life of Charlotte Brontë — Volume 1,Elizabeth Cleghorn Gaskell,,Biography,"The Leeds and Skipton railway runs along a deep valley of the Aire; a slow and sluggish stream, compared to the neighbouring river of Wharfe. Keighley station is on this line of railway, about a quarter of a mile from the town of the same name. The number of inhabitants and the importance of Keighley have been very greatly increased during the last twenty years, owing to the rapidly extended market for worsted manufactures, a branch of industry that mainly employs the factory population of this part of Yorkshire, which has Bradford for its centre and metropolis.",1865,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/ff/f8/08/fff80874-7701-112a-5400-3c2a3694c2b6/coverArt.551ad3.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"The Leeds and Skipton railway runs along a deep valley of the Aire; a slow and sluggish stream, compared to the neighbouring river of Wharfe. Keighley station is on this line of railway, about a quarter of a mile from the town of the same name. The number of inhabitants and the importance of Keighley have been very greatly increased during the last twenty years, owing to the rapidly extended market for worsted manufactures, a branch of industry that mainly employs the factory population of this ...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/life-of-charlotte-bront%C3%AB-volume-1/id501613792?uo=4,
9eafe742,The Pretty Sister Of Jos?,Frances Hodgson Burnett,,Short Stories,"This is a romantic drama novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett . Jose was a poor hardworking labour , who lived with his aged grandmother and sister Pepita . José fell into the way of planning to escape from all this, and make another home for himself and his pretty child-sister and the old woman. He knew there was only one way to do it: if he could carry his one gift where it would be of more use to him than it could possibly be in a poor small village; if he could carry it to a market where there were more people and where work was better paid for.",1889,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication1/v4/82/1e/97/821e9737-3e63-3638-0b92-9079776fb649/coverArt.cf5b3a.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"This is a romantic drama novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett . Jose was a poor hardworking labour , who lived with his aged grandmother and sister Pepita . José fell into the way of planning to escape from all this, and make another home for himself and his pretty child-sister and the old woman. He knew there was only one way to do it: if he could carry his one gift where it would be of more use to him than it could possibly be in a poor small village; if he could carry it to a market where there w...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/the-pretty-sister-of-jos/id510910048?uo=4,
821178e7,A March on London,George Alfred Henty,,Historical Fiction,"The events that took place during the latter half of the fourteenth century and the first half of the fifteenth are known to us far better than those preceding or following them, owing to the fact that three great chroniclers, Froissart, Monstrelet, and Holinshed, have recounted the events with a fulness of detail that leaves nothing to be desired. The uprising of the Commons, as they called themselves—that is to say, chiefly the folk who were still kept in a state of serfdom in the reign of Richard II. —was in itself justifiable. Although serfdom in England was never carried to the extent that prevailed on the Continent, the serfs suffered from grievous disabilities. A certain portion of their time had to be devoted to the work of their feudal lord. They themselves were forbidden to buy or sell at public markets or fairs.",1902,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/d5/49/65/d5496559-5d94-9649-0911-035561d1c736/coverArt.01e65c.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"The events that took place during the latter half of the fourteenth century and the first half of the fifteenth are known to us far better than those preceding or following them, owing to the fact that three great chroniclers, Froissart, Monstrelet, and Holinshed, have recounted the events with a fulness of detail that leaves nothing to be desired. The uprising of the Commons, as they called themselves—that is to say, chiefly the folk who were still kept in a state of serfdom in the reign of Ric...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/a-march-on-london/id506034622?uo=4,
797c4d51,Burma,Robert Talbot Kelly,,Asian History,The book provides a visual and textual account of colonial Burma that was subsequently marketed in England and America. Travelogues served as a form of voyeuristic education about the exotic for the stay-at-home adventurer.,2008,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication5/v4/6a/1f/a8/6a1fa891-f44a-35cf-7bd0-050fadd8e75d/coverArt.d2e9ff.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,The book provides a visual and textual account of colonial Burma that was subsequently marketed in England and America. Travelogues served as a form of voyeuristic education about the exotic for the stay-at-home adventurer.,False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/burma/id511230234?uo=4,
bae1a013,The Man from Archangel,Arthur Conan Doyle,,Mystery Short Stories,"Set in a small market town in France, this is a bleak story of prejudice, isolation and loneliness. Jonas Milk is a Russian Jew who runs a second-hand book shop and leads a quiet unassuming life. Married to a promiscuous younger French woman, he wakes one day to find she has disappeared. Assuming she has run off with another man for a few days, as she has done before, Jonas tells his neighbours and his wife’s family that she has gone to visit a friend. When the wife fails to return as expected people begin to suspect him of murdering her. Rather than admit his wife’s previous infidelities, the little man maintains his lie in the face of increasing hostility and isolation until he is driven to despair.",1930,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/8e/bf/85/8ebf85b2-ec09-5737-cb9d-bc571ce8732b/coverArt.162e97.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"Set in a small market town in France, this is a bleak story of prejudice, isolation and loneliness. Jonas Milk is a Russian Jew who runs a second-hand book shop and leads a quiet unassuming life. Married to a promiscuous younger French woman, he wakes one day to find she has disappeared. Assuming she has run off with another man for a few days, as she has done before, Jonas tells his neighbours and his wife’s family that she has gone to visit a friend. When the wife fails to return as expected p...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/the-man-from-archangel/id492566805?uo=4,
a88ffac4,Lost,Edward Bellamy,,Fiction & Literature,"The 25th of May, 1866, was no doubt to many a quite indifferent date, but to two persons it was the saddest day of their lives. Charles Randall that day left Bonn, Germany, to catch the steamer home to America, and Ida Werner was left with a mountain of grief on her gentle bosom, which must be melted away drop by drop, in tears, before she could breathe freely again. A year before, Randall, hunting for apartments, his last term at the university just begun, had seen the announcement, "" Zimmer zu vermiethen, "" in the hall below the flat where the Werners lived. Ida answered his ring, for her father was still at his government office, and her mother had gone out to the market to buy the supper. She would much rather her mother had been at home to show the gentleman the rooms; but, knowing that they could not afford to lose a chance to rent them, she plucked up courage, and, candle in hand, showed him through the suite.",1898,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication1/v4/fd/f3/4a/fdf34a4c-9e69-67f5-bde2-6804857c64b7/coverArt.7a5bf6.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"The 25th of May, 1866, was no doubt to many a quite indifferent date, but to two persons it was the saddest day of their lives. Charles Randall that day left Bonn, Germany, to catch the steamer home to America, and Ida Werner was left with a mountain of grief on her gentle bosom, which must be melted away drop by drop, in tears, before she could breathe freely again. A year before, Randall, hunting for apartments, his last term at the university just begun, had seen the announcement, "" Zimmer zu...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/lost/id511149613?uo=4,
76df6db4,Captains of Industry,James Parton,,Design,"During the Industrial Revolution, a captain of industry was a business leader whose means of amassing a personal fortune contributes positively to the country in some way. This may have been through increased productivity, expansion of markets, providing more jobs, or acts of philanthropy. This characterization contrasts with that of the robber baron, a business leader using political means to achieve his ends.",1891,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication5/v4/80/58/aa/8058aa9a-c73f-be31-9b53-a01ff8208851/coverArt.f95ad0.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"During the Industrial Revolution, a captain of industry was a business leader whose means of amassing a personal fortune contributes positively to the country in some way. This may have been through increased productivity, expansion of markets, providing more jobs, or acts of philanthropy. This characterization contrasts with that of the robber baron, a business leader using political means to achieve his ends.",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/captains-of-industry/id511124122?uo=4,
d5c48629,Travels in the Interior of Africa — Volume 02,Mungo Park,,African History,"Travels in the Interior of Africa — Volume 02 is a historical book. Extends only to reasonable correction; for the master cannot sell his domestic, without having first brought him to a public trial before the chief men of the place. But these restrictions on the power of the master extend not to the care of prisoners taken in war, nor to that of slaves purchased with money. All these unfortunate beings are considered as strangers and foreigners, who have no right to the protection of the law, and may be treated with severity, or sold to a stranger, according to the pleasure of their owners. There are, indeed, regular markets, where slaves of this description are bought and sold, and the value of a slave, in the eye of an African purchaser, increases in proportion to his distance from his native kingdom.",1806,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/75/dc/83/75dc83c6-0bb6-58b1-9623-0a1a24ffe87d/coverArt.768165.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"Travels in the Interior of Africa — Volume 02 is a historical book. Extends only to reasonable correction; for the master cannot sell his domestic, without having first brought him to a public trial before the chief men of the place. But these restrictions on the power of the master extend not to the care of prisoners taken in war, nor to that of slaves purchased with money. All these unfortunate beings are considered as strangers and foreigners, who have no right to the protection of the law, a...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/travels-in-the-interior-of-africa-volume-02/id500614894?uo=4,
95b0e732,"The Interest of America in Sea Power, Present and Future",Alfred Thayer Mahan,,Military History,"Indications are not wanting of an approaching change in the thoughts and policy of Americans as to their relations with the world outside their own borders. For the past quarter of a century, the predominant idea, which has asserted itself successfully at the polls and shaped the course of the government, has been to preserve the home market for the home industries. The employer and the workman alike have been taught to look at the various economical measures proposed from this point of view, to regard with hostility any step favoring the intrusion of the foreign producer upon their own domain, and rather to demand increasingly rigorous measures of exclusion than to acquiesce in any loosening of the chain that binds the consumer to them.",1897,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/32/a1/d9/32a1d9f9-91f9-114f-7ced-35f30ff7f48d/coverArt.f0d1c1.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"Indications are not wanting of an approaching change in the thoughts and policy of Americans as to their relations with the world outside their own borders. For the past quarter of a century, the predominant idea, which has asserted itself successfully at the polls and shaped the course of the government, has been to preserve the home market for the home industries. The employer and the workman alike have been taught to look at the various economical measures proposed from this point of view, to...",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/the-interest-of-america-in-sea-power-present-and-future/id509768139?uo=4,
61a646e8,In the Fire of the Forge — Volume 04,Georg Ebers,,Fiction & Literature,"The city gates were already open. Peasants and peasant women bringing vegetables and other farm produce to market thronged the streets, wains loaded with grain or charcoal rumbled along, and herds of cattle and swine, laden donkeys, the little carts of the farmers and bee keepers conveying milk and honey to the city, passed over the dyke, which was still softened by the rain of the preceding night.",1898,,,250,Tiếng Việt,Ebook,https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Publication7/v4/dc/c8/15/dcc81537-8b2c-9db6-e832-ccd40d3c6f51/coverArt.cbab7b.jpg/600x600bb.jpg,4.5,False,marketing,Mọi độc giả,Tích cực,Trung bình,"The city gates were already open. Peasants and peasant women bringing vegetables and other farm produce to market thronged the streets, wains loaded with grain or charcoal rumbled along, and herds of cattle and swine, laden donkeys, the little carts of the farmers and bee keepers conveying milk and honey to the city, passed over the dyke, which was still softened by the rain of the preceding night.",False,,,,https://books.apple.com/vn/book/in-the-fire-of-the-forge-volume-04/id500619712?uo=4,
